ere the omis logic africa  and working hard to advance the omis  omislogic training across  africa  so the omislogic sets of bioinformatics  and big data analysis training programs  of the prime biotech incorporated which  has been globally proven by peer reviews  and curriculum experts in partnering  stations is being eventually explored in  closing the needed gaps  with regards to bioinformatics education  and training  globally  of course this is of great importance  for us here in africa in terms of  building  these scientific capacities among  students  researchers young scholars young  professionals  and faculties across the  african continent  and so um the postulation rather um with  omisologic africa that is anchored by  eureka is that by increasingly advancing  the knowledge of bioinformatics and in  its use in obtaining scientific insights  from sequence data there will be a  significant growth and development of  the bioinformatics community here in  africa and its considerable implications  for translational science from  understanding of gene functions  as well as its ruling biology  agricultural medicine means just um a  variety of feeds uh for addressing  challenges that are peculiar to the  population here within the continent and  so the goal of homeless loyalty programs  therefore is to provide this training in  bioinformatics  by enabling students clinicians and  faculty of all backgrounds to  develop novel and independent research  that is guided by mentors and peer  examples and so the omis logic programs  boost of everything the participant  needs to get started and grow in the  bioinformatics and big data analysis  space for scientific research and  practice  our programs combine online interactive  sections and self-guided study materials  and practical assignments for an  immersive experience proven to have been  very effective in our well-known and  respected mixed logic bioinformatics and  training programs so um while the  growing interest in bioinformatics and  big data analysis continues to grow here  in africa many are still far from being  able to gain this key set for  utilization in their scientific research  um  as well as practice but we are glad that  we do miss logic africa training  programs of primeval 10 corporate these  gaps are being breached for students  faculties and researchers across the  african continent and so i'd like to  quickly share  here a few of such programs which over  the course of the past 12 months we have  organized um you know to bring  bioinformatics training with project  guided learning and resources to a  cross-section of participants across  you know the continent ranging from  beginners and students many of whom are  new to bioinformatics to  postgraduates as well as researchers and  faculties wanting to develop skills and  research capacity to explore the world  of umic sciences and using  bioinformatics and big data analysis to  answer research questions so um this  high training of course includes data  science for biologists introduction to  bioinformatics  as well as  with bioinformatics and computational  biology and also we've gone into  bioinformatics for biomedical drug  discovery these are some of the programs  we've run lately  and equally  at least test program is the umix logic  training for students and researchers  which is a basic bioinformatics  introductory workshop and i was recently  concluded and this  program actually had over 200  participants who participated and gained  the requisite skill to get introduced  and to get introduced into the  bioinformatics space  equally we recently conducted homicide  genomics workshop  which we just concluded and it's amazing  the outcome we got from these programs  as we have currently a number of  participants moving on currently into  our research fellowship program so this  training is essentially prepares these  participants and some of the training  program participants  who have gone from being beginners in  bioinformatics to learning requisite  skill sets that they can apply into  their own personal research and practice  um include stem multi um um some of the  um you know  of the things that these participants  have learned and equally acquired a  number of expertise in a cross section  of um  domains  learning domains on our learning  platform equally we have ubisola a  pharmaceutical microbiologist who has  seen her practice on application of keep  informatics concept in her practice  significantly um enhanced and um in  addition to that we have jason lee  florida from cameroon who now sees  ourselves  well prepared to take on our research  and you know journey into the marine  biology studies space leveraging on kids  cases from our mixed logic um  informatics trainings  so surface to say that and we have also  forged notable partnerships with  institutions towards integrating our  hands-on  mentor-driven globally proven training  methods and resources into university  education across africa  both at undergraduate as well as  postgraduate levels and just to help  scale rapidly the growth our capacity of  bioinformatics researches and  you know um across the continent and so  few of such notable partnerships include  you know partners we listed university  in nigeria  we also have a partnership with  crescent university as well as ocean  state university and most most  much recently we had a working  relationship in with  university of yandee that is in cameroon  similarly mislogic africa team has  participated at notable regional  scientific workshops uh such as the  nigerian bioinformatics and genomics  network where we had a poster  presentation on the topic experimenting  with  21st century e-learning design for  bridging bioinformatics education gaps  in africa a test case with mislogic  activity rubrics  and moving along i'd like to quickly  mention our next  training program that is around the  corner uh which is another introductory  bioin